## Latest Developments in Artificial Intelligence

Based on recent reporting from The Verge, TechCrunch, VentureBeat, and Google's official blog, here are the most significant latest developments in AI:

### 🏢 Major Industry Moves & Acquisitions
- **SpaceX acquired AI coding tool Cursor** in a **$60 billion** deal — the company says Cursor will work on its Grok AI chatbot.
- **Stripe is reportedly acquiring AI gateway startup OpenRouter** for **$7B+**.
- **Cognition** (AI coding startup) is reportedly in talks to raise at a **$40B valuation**.
- **Lovable** confirmed a **$13.3B valuation**, raising another $400M.
- **Databricks** raised **$5B at a $190B valuation** (investors wanted to give $15B).
- **Wispr** raised **$280M at a $2B valuation** for AI voice/dictation tech.
- **Nvidia** unveiled a new **$500B plan** focused on data centers and aging GPU infrastructure.
- **IBM partnered with OpenAI** to bolster its enterprise AI push.

### 🧠 Frontier Model Launches & Updates
- **Google's Gemini 3.7 Flash** is now available in AI Mode for Search, offering improved instruction-following, and is notably competitive in coding and agent workloads at a lower price tier. (Google still hasn't launched its long-overdue 3.5 Pro model.)
- **Grok 4.6** launched with frontier-level intelligence, major gains over the prior generation, and stronger long-running agent behavior.
- **OpenAI introduced "Ultrafast" mode**, making **GPT-5.6 Sol** run at **14x speed**.
- **Writer** launched a new AI model (Palmyra X6) with a "harness" that cuts agent costs by **52%** and improves speed by **48%**.
- **Anthropic's Claude** received new invisible text watermarks, using a version of Google's open-source **SynthID-Text** system.

### 🤖 The Agentic AI Era
- **Google I/O 2026** was themed "Welcome to the **agentic Gemini era**" — with **1 billion+ people** using the Gemini app monthly.
- **Grok Bot** launched, packaging computer use, persistence, workflow learning, and multi-agent coordination into a "workforce interface."
- **Anthropic's Claude in Chrome is now "Claude Cowork"** — an agent that saves chats and continues tasks across desktop, web, and mobile.
- Google released **Gemini API Managed Agents (3.6 Flash)** with hooks.
- Notably, Anthropic tested **AI agents on the same task and they started a "turf war"** — highlighting emerging multi-agent coordination challenges.

### 🏥 AI in Science & Medicine
- **Google's AMIE** medical AI system demonstrated **real-time clinical video consultation** capabilities in a first-of-its-kind study.
- Google is applying AI breakthroughs for **crisis resilience**.

### ⚖️ Safety, Regulation & Trust
- **OpenAI reportedly disbanded its preparedness team** — the latest shakeup of its safety teams as it heads toward an IPO.
- **Anthropic's CEO** says the AI backlash is "fundamentally a **crisis of trust**."
- **Anthropic will watermark text** generated by its AI models, sparking user backlash over workplace detection.
- **Google now allows users to remove visible watermarks** from AI-generated images.
- Three AI pioneers made the case for **staying open** amid rising safety concerns.

### 💼 Enterprise & Productivity
- **OpenAI's enterprise revenue has surpassed consumer revenue** (CFO confirmed lines have crossed).
- **Microsoft is merging its separate Copilot apps** into a "super app" and killing off unsuccessful AI features.
- **IBM + OpenAI** enterprise partnership.
- **Google Meet** now has AI notetaking for **in-person meetings** (audio → Gemini-generated notes, transcripts, action items).
- **OpenAI-backed Thrive Holdings** raised **$2B** to bring AI to the enterprise.

### 📱 Consumer AI & Platforms
- **Apple** trained its own AI model for China with help from **Alibaba**, and is in talks to **pay publishers** so Siri can deliver news.
- **YouTube's "Ask" AI chatbot search** rolled out to mobile.
- **Twitch** now trains Amazon's generative AI models on streamers' content **by default** (opt-out), drawing criticism.
- Amazon is reportedly **buying used/rare books in bulk**, cutting bindings off to scan them faster for AI training data.
- **ChatGPT's Computer History** now tracks your clicks and keystrokes.
- **Google's Pixel 11 event** featured extensive Gemini integrations.

### ⚡ Infrastructure
- Massive **AI data center buildouts** are popping up across the US, frequently facing local opposition.
- **Hyperscalers** are embracing natural gas for AI data centers, though a new forecast warns they may regret it.

---

**Bottom line:** The field is moving at breakneck speed toward **agentic AI** (models that take actions, use tools, and coordinate), with a massive wave of consolidation (SpaceX-Cursor, Stripe-OpenRouter), enterprise revenue outpacing consumer, new frontier models from Google, xAI, and OpenAI, and growing debates over **trust, watermarks, and safety governance** as AI becomes embedded in nearly every product.

*Note: Search queries via DuckDuckGo were temporarily blocked, so this summary is compiled from direct fetches of The Verge, TechCrunch, VentureBeat, and Google's AI blog — which together provide excellent, current coverage.*
